Which adjacency matrix correctly represents this undirected network?
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2.8,2.2);
\coordinate (C) at (2.8,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.25, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[pos=0.75, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$7$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$4$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The directed network diagram shows connections between four nodes $A, B, C, D$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.6 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2.8,2.2);
\coordinate (C) at (2.8,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$3$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$5$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$4$};
\draw[midarrow] (C) -- (A) node[pos=0.25, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw[midarrow] (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$6$};
\draw[midarrow] (D) -- (B) node[pos=0.75, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$1$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
What is the entry in **row $C$, column $A$** of the adjacency matrix?

The diagram shows an undirected network. The weights are distances in kilometres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,2.4);
\coordinate (C) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway,above] {$14$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.25,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$16$};
\draw (A) -- (D) node[midway,left] {$18$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway,right] {$9$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[pos=0.25,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$13$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway,below] {$11$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{array}{c|cccc} \text{From/To} & A & B & C & D \\ \hline A & - & 14 & x & 18 \\ B & 14 & - & 9 & y \\ C & x & 9 & - & 11 \\ D & 18 & y & 11 & - \end{array}$
Which values complete the table?
